sec.p:
To quantify the expected choice accuracy and reward expectation, we used previous methods (Fan et al., 2024). Specifically, we defined choice accuracy as the estimated accuracy, on average, given the current choice and decision time (DT), as following:
(Eq.2)
Choice accuracy={P(Correct∣Right,DT),Right target is chosen at DTP(Correct∣Left,DT),Left target is chosen at DT \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \text { Choice accuracy }=\left\{\begin{array}{r} P(\text { Correct } \mid \text { Right,DT }), \text { Right target is chosen at DT } \tag{Eq.2}\\ P(\text { Correct } \mid \text { Left,DT }), \text { Left target is chosen at DT } \end{array}\right.$$\end{document}
where DT is the decision time that equals RT minus non-decision time (estimated from DDM fits). The righthand side was computed by marginalizing over all possible coherences. For example, for Right choices,
(Eq.3)
P(Correct∣Right,DT)=∑Cohi[P(Correct∣Right,DT,Cohi)P(Cohi∣Right,DT)]=∑CohiP(CorrectRight,DT,Cohi)P(Righti,DT∣Cohi)P(Cohi)∑Cohi[P(Right,DT∣Cohi)P(Cohi)] \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{align*} & P(\text { Correct } \mid \text { Right }, D T)=\sum_{\operatorname{Coh}_{i}}\left[P\left(\text { Correct } \mid \text { Right, } D T, \operatorname{Coh}_{i}\right) P\left(\operatorname{Coh}_{i} \mid \text { Right, } D T\right)\right] \tag{Eq.3}\\ & =\sum_{\operatorname{Coh}_{i}} \frac{P\left(\operatorname{Correct}^{\text {Right }}, D T, \operatorname{Coh}_{i}\right) P\left(\operatorname{Right}_{i}, D T \mid \operatorname{Coh}_{i}\right) P\left(\operatorname{Coh}_{i}\right)}{\sum_{\operatorname{Coh}_{i}}\left[P\left(\text { Right, } D T \mid \operatorname{Coh}_{i}\right) P\left(\operatorname{Coh}_{i}\right)\right]} \end{align*}$$\end{document}
By task design,
(Eq.4)
P(Correct∣Right,DT, Coh i)={1 if 2 Coh i>00if Coh i<0 \begin{document}$$\displaystyle P\left(\text { Correct } \mid \text { Right }, D T, \text { Coh }_{i}\right)=\left\{\begin{array}{cc} 1 & \text { if }^{2} \text { Coh }_{i}>0 \tag{Eq.4}\\ 0 & \text { if } \text { Coh }_{i}<0 \end{array}\right.$$\end{document}
P(Right,DT|Cohi) was obtained by numerical simulation of the DDM using the best-fitting parameters. For each coherence, we obtained the probability of the decision variable (DV) attaining a value x at time t, pdfDv(t) = P(DV(t) = x |Cohi), using the best fitting DDM parameters of each session and reward context.
(Eq.5)
P(Right,DT∣ Coh i)=∫upper bound∞P(DV(t)=x∣ Coh i)dxP(Left,DT∣ Coh i)=∫−∞lower boundP(DV(t)=x∣ Coh i)dx \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{align*} & P\left(\text { Right }, D T \mid \text { Coh }_{i}\right)=\int_{\text {upper bound }}^{\infty} P\left(D V(t)=x \mid \text { Coh }_{i}\right) d x \tag{Eq.5}\\ & P\left(\text { Left }, \quad D T \mid \text { Coh }_{i}\right)=\int_{-\infty}^{\text {lower bound }} P\left(D V(t)=x \mid \text { Coh }_{i}\right) d x \end{align*}$$\end{document}
After obtaining an estimate of choice accuracy,
(Eq.6)
Reward Expectation=Accuracy × Reward size associated with the choiceReward size={1if small rewardlarge/smallif large reward \begin{document}$$\displaystyle = \begin{cases}1 & \text { if small reward } \\ \text { large/small } & \text { if large reward }\end{cases}$$\end{document}

All analyses were performed on activity on the asymmetric-reward task. Only correct trials were included for neural activity analysis to avoid the confound of potential task disengagement during error trials. To relate activity to decision-related factors, we performed two regression analyses. First, for each single unit, we computed the average firing rates in seven task epochs (Figure 1A): 1) a 400 ms window beginning at target onset (focusing on visual response to target presentation), 2) a 200 ms window ending at dots onset (focusing on activity before motion viewing), 3) a 300 ms window beginning at 100 ms after dots onset (focusing on early motion viewing), 4) a variable-duration window from 100 ms after motion onset to 100 ms before saccade onset (focusing on the whole motion viewing period), 5) a 300 ms window ending at saccade onset (late motion viewing, pre-saccade activity), 6) a 300 ms window beginning at 100 ms prior to saccade onset (peri-saccade activity), and 7) a 400 ms window beginning at saccade onset (post-saccade activity). We performed a multiple linear regression on the spike counts from correct trials, for each task epoch separately.
(Eq.7)
Spike count=β0+βChoice×IChoice+βRewCont×IRewCont+βRewSize×IRewSize+βCoh-Contra×ICoh-Contra+βCoh-Ipsi×ICoh-Ipsi+βRewCoh-Contra×ICoh-Contra×IRewSize+βRewCoh-Ipsi×ICoh-Ipsi×IRewSize, \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{align*} & \text { Spike count }=\beta_{0}+\beta_{\text {Choice }} \times I_{\text {Choice }}+\beta_{\text {RewCont }} \times I_{\text {RewCont }}+\beta_{\text {RewSize }} \times I_{\text {RewSize }} \\ & \quad+\beta_{\text {Coh-Contra }} \times I_{\text {Coh-Contra }}+\beta_{\text {Coh-Ipsi }} \times I_{\text {Coh-Ipsi }} \\ & +\beta_{\text {RewCoh-Contra }} \times I_{\text {Coh-Contra }} \times I_{\text {RewSize }}+\beta_{\text {RewCoh-Ipsi }} \times I_{\text {Coh-Ipsi }} \times I_{\text {RewSize }}, \tag{Eq.7} \end{align*}$$\end{document}
where
IChoice={1contralateral choice−1ipsilateral choiceIRewCont={1contralateral-large reward−1ipsilateral choice-large rewardIRewSize={1large reward is expected−1small reward is expectedICoh-Contra={cohcontralateral choice0ipsilateral choiceICoh-Ipsi={0contralateral choiceCohipsilateral choice \begin{document}$\begin{array}{l}I_{\text {Choice }}=\left\{\begin{array}{ll}1 & \text { contralateral choice } \\ -1 & \text { ipsilateral choice }\end{array}\right. \\ I_{\text {RewCont }}=\left\{\begin{array}{rc}1 & \text { contralateral-large reward } \\ -1 & \text { ipsilateral choice-large reward }\end{array}\right. \\ I_{\text {RewSize }}=\left\{\begin{array}{ll}1 & \text { large reward is expected } \\ -1 & \text { small reward is expected }\end{array}\right. \\ I_{\text {Coh-Contra }}=\left\{\begin{array}{ll}\text { coh } & \text { contralateral choice } \\ 0 & \text { ipsilateral choice }\end{array}\right. \\ I_{\text {Coh-Ipsi }}=\left\{\begin{array}{lc}0 & \text { contralateral choice } \\ \text { Coh } & \text { ipsilateral choice }\end{array}\right.\end{array}$\end{document}
